    "created_at": "2024-10-23T11:12:32Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-10-23T12:47:50Z",
    "body": "> origin: a new opaque origin?? Will this break Fetch and cause various security checks to fail?? Maybe we should pick the target URL's origin instead?\r\n\r\n[edited]\r\nI looked through various specs, like service workers and fetch metadata. I couldn't find one place where the origin of a \r\nbrowser-initiated navigation request is observable. So perhaps it doesn't really matter what we put there, and an opaque origin makes the most sense?",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
